---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Nexus Wave Technologies">
  <section class="hero legal-hero"><div class="container post-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy & Safety</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">This policy explains how Nexus Wave Technologies handles information across the public website, private support services, Nexus Plus integrations and team programmes.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container legal-shell"><nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal pages"><a href="/legal/privacy" aria-current="page">Privacy</a><a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a><a href="/legal/refund">Refunds</a><a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a><a href="/legal/accessibility">Accessibility</a></nav><article class="prose card legal-document">
    <h2>1. What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>This policy applies to the Nexus Wave Technologies public website, product information pages, contact forms and services that are explicitly described on the website.</p>

    <h2>2. Information we may receive</h2>
    <p>Depending on the feature you use, we may receive a display name, account identifier, verified phone number, email address, support-case information, messages, notification preferences, team application details and technical information needed to keep the service secure.</p>
    <p>For a private Women Safety complaint submitted from the website, a contact email address or phone number may be required so that we can provide a safe follow-up route when the person is not using Nexus Plus. If you are already a Nexus Plus user and the system can securely match your verified account, you may use the app-based contact route instead of re-entering contact details.</p>

    <h2>3. Product and support information</h2><p>Information you submit through a contact or support form is used to respond to your request, provide the requested service, maintain security and meet applicable legal obligations. We do not ask you to submit passwords, OTPs or full payment-card details through ordinary contact forms.</p>

    <h2>4. Payment information</h2><p>When you purchase a paid service, payment details are handled by the configured payment provider rather than being stored as full card credentials in ordinary website code. Transaction records needed for billing, refunds, fraud prevention and legal compliance may be retained for the applicable period.</p>

    <h2>5. Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures such as HTTPS/TLS, access controls and protected service credentials. No internet service can provide an absolute zero-risk guarantee.</p>

    <h2>6. Third-party services</h2><p>Supabase, payment providers and other service providers may process limited information needed to operate requested features. Their own terms and privacy policies may also apply.</p>

    <h2>7. Data minimisation and retention</h2>
    <p>We aim to delete temporary or operational data that is no longer needed within 24 hours where technically feasible and lawful. Private complaint records are intended to be retained for no longer than 5 days unless a longer period is required by law, an active support process, a security investigation, or another clearly documented necessity.</p>
    <p>Attachments, temporary processing objects, invitation tokens and unused operational records should be expired or removed as soon as they are no longer needed. Supabase Storage and database cleanup should follow the same retention policy rather than leaving stale copies behind.</p>

    <h2>8. Your choices</h2><p>Where applicable, you may request access, correction or deletion of personal information. Some records may need to be retained for legal, security, fraud-prevention or transaction-record purposes.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2><p>As Nexus services evolve, this policy may be updated. The current version will remain published on this page.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@nexusweb.co.in">info@nexusweb.co.in</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 1, 2026.</p>
  </article></div></section>
<style is:global>
  .legal-hero{padding:72px 0 40px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--color-surface),var(--color-bg))}
  .legal-hero .lead{max-width:760px}
  .legal-shell{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px;align-items:start}
  .legal-nav{position:sticky;top:96px;display:grid;gap:6px;padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:16px;background:var(--color-surface)}
  .legal-nav a{padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;color:var(--color-text-muted);text-decoration:none;font-size:.92rem;font-weight:650}
  .legal-nav a:hover,.legal-nav a[aria-current=page]{background:var(--color-surface-soft);color:var(--color-text)}
  .legal-document{padding:32px}
  .legal-document h2{margin:34px 0 10px;font-size:1.35rem}
  .legal-document h2:first-child{margin-top:0}
  .legal-document p{margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.75}
  .legal-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:20px}
  .legal-meta span{padding:7px 10px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:999px;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-text-muted)}
  @media(max-width:850px){.legal-shell{grid-template-columns:1fr}.legal-nav{position:static;display:flex;overflow:auto}.legal-nav a{flex:0 0 auto}.legal-document{padding:24px}}
</style>
</Layout>